ADR 0007 D3: open the PR, then immediately run `gh pr merge <n> --squash --auto`. Spec 28 D7 (line 74) and §7.5 (line 256) change this for the bootstrap session's PRs:
- auto-merge waits for a pr-gate go;
- it is pinned with `--match-head-commit`;
- D4-protected PRs and P0/P4 go to the user.
The ADR 0007 bullet in ADR 0021's relationship section (line 60) only says repo-level auto-merge and branch protection stay the same. This is a scoped amendment of an ADR process decision, made in a spec, not an ADR being overturned. One clause in that bullet naming the D7 precondition would keep the relationship explicit for the next reader of ADR 0007.
